          "end": 50.49,
          "en": "getting-started-with-nextjs Markdown file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.49,
          "end": 52.97,
          "en": "And you can replace your existing one with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.97,
          "end": 54.68,
          "en": "It has the same metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.68,
          "end": 57.95,
          "en": "but different content, just some dummy content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.95,
          "end": 60.06,
          "en": "with a list, another title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.06,
          "end": 62.15,
          "en": "and also with an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.15,
          "end": 65.6,
          "en": "This is how you include a image in Markdown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 65.6,
          "end": 67.95,
          "en": "The problem is if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 67.95,
          "end": 71.77,
          "en": "and you reload this page, the image is not showing up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.77,
          "end": 74.14,
          "en": "because the path is incorrect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.14,
          "end": 75.5,
          "en": "Now, we could fix the path here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 75.5,
          "end": 77.91,
          "en": "and change it to images/post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 77.91,
          "end": 80.72,
          "en": "and then our Slack,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 80.72,
          "end": 83.187,
          "en": "so getting-started-with-nextjs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.34,
          "end": 86.51,
          "en": "Make sure you have no typos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 86.51,
          "end": 88.27,
          "en": "And then also add that image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.27,
          "end": 89.91,
          "en": "which you also find attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 89.91,
          "end": 91.81,
          "en": "You also need to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 91.81,
          "end": 95.53999999999999,
          "en": "Attached, you find a Next.js file-based routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 95.53999999999999,
          "end": 97.28999999999999,
          "en": "PNG dummy image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "which you can also add to your posts folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 102.5,
          "en": "in the images folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 102.5,
          "end": 105.65299999999999,
          "en": "So to this specific posts folder there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 106.78,
          "end": 108.74000000000001,
          "en": "Now this path should be correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 108.74000000000001,
          "end": 111.22999999999999,
          "en": "Oops, that should be posts though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 111.22999999999999,
          "end": 113.09,
          "en": "but if you check for all typos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 113.09,
          "end": 114.146,
          "en": "it should be correct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 114.146,
          "end": 117.68,
          "en": "and if you reload now, you should see the image here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 117.68,
          "end": 119.35,
          "en": "but we have a couple of problems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 119.35,
          "end": 120.83,
          "en": "Clearly it's too big.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 120.83,
          "end": 122.29,
          "en": "It's not styled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 122.29,
          "end": 123.66,
          "en": "Now, we could style it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 125,
          "en": "That wouldn't be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 125,
          "end": 128.61,
          "en": "We could style it by simply adjusting the styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 128.61,
          "end": 131.2,
          "en": "in the post-content.module file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 131.2,
          "end": 133.79,
          "en": "We could target image elements here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 133.79,
          "end": 138.24,
          "en": "and for example, give them a max-width of 200 pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 138.24,
          "end": 139.52,
          "en": "or something like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 139.52,
          "end": 141.31,
          "en": "and now it would be smaller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 141.31,
          "end": 144.03,
          "en": "So that is a problem which we can solve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 144.03,
          "end": 145.31,
          "en": "I'll get rid of this though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 145.31,
          "end": 147.09,
          "en": "But that's something we could solve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 147.09,
          "end": 150.07999999999998,
          "en": "The bigger problem is that we're not taking advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 150.07999999999998,
          "end": 153.52,
          "en": "of Next.js image optimizations here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 153.52,
          "end": 154.69,
          "en": "If we inspect this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 154.69,
          "end": 156.98,
          "en": "we see that it's a regular image element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 156.98,
          "end": 158.8,
          "en": "which is being rendered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 158.8,
          "end": 161.41,
          "en": "And that is okay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 161.41,
          "end": 164.86,
          "en": "but we give up on all the optimization potential.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 164.86,
          "end": 168.57,
          "en": "For example, this is a huge image file, it's huge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 168.57,
          "end": 170.87,
          "en": "and even if I change the size in CSS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 170.87,
          "end": 173.73,
          "en": "we still load this original file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 173.73,
          "end": 176.09,
          "en": "And that's definitely not what we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 176.09,
          "end": 178.64,
          "en": "Lazy loading would also be nice to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 178.64,
          "end": 180.63,
          "en": "because the image is not even visible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 180.63,
          "end": 182.85,
          "en": "when we start reading this post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 184.38,
          "en": "and therefore, it would be great",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 184.38,
          "end": 187.51,
          "en": "if it is only loaded once we scroll there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 187.51,
          "end": 190.92,
          "en": "And that's all something next/image does for us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 190.92,
          "end": 192.38,
          "en": "but not right now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 192.38,
          "end": 196.59,
          "en": "because by default, react-markdown translates an image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 196.59,
          "end": 199.73,
          "en": "in the Markdown file, so translates code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 199.73,
          "end": 201.9,
          "en": "into a regular image tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 201.9,
          "end": 203.31,
          "en": "and that makes a lot of sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 203.31,
          "end": 206.25,
          "en": "because how would it know that you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 206.25,
          "end": 209.89,
          "en": "to have your own image transformation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 209.89,
          "end": 212.45,
          "en": "that you want to use a different component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 212.45,
          "end": 215.53,
          "en": "It doesn't know that but you can tell it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 215.53,
          "end": 217.37,
          "en": "And therefore, first of all, I'll get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 217.37,
          "end": 222.37,
          "en": "of that path here and just stick to the image file name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 222.63,
          "end": 224.69,
          "en": "because we will now override",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 224.69,
          "end": 229.09,
          "en": "how react-markdown treats Markdown content like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 229.09,
          "end": 231.09,
          "en": "how it treats images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 231.09,
          "end": 234.45,
          "en": "To override how certain elements are rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 234.45,
          "end": 237.75,
          "en": "we can give react-markdown a special prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 237.75,
          "end": 241.03,
          "en": "the renderers prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 241.03,
          "end": 243.26,
          "en": "Renderers wants an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 243.26,
          "end": 245.9,
          "en": "where you tell react-markdown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 245.9,
          "end": 248.5,
          "en": "how certain elements should be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 248.5,
          "end": 251.06,
          "en": "Now, you can't come up with your own elements here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 251.06,
          "end": 253.49,
          "en": "Instead, there are built-in elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 253.49,
          "end": 255.53,
          "en": "where you can override the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 255.53,
          "end": 258.95,
          "en": "The react-markdown documentation is the place to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 258.95,
          "end": 260.47,
          "en": "for more details.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 260.47,
          "end": 263.36,
          "en": "There you find detailed usage instructions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 263.36,
          "end": 265.57,
          "en": "You can also configure other things there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 265.57,
          "end": 269.076,
          "en": "and there, you also get like a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 269.076,
          "end": 272.89,
          "en": "of the different elements it's able to render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 272.89,
          "end": 276.033,
          "en": "and the identifier in renderers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 277.13,
          "end": 278.99,
          "en": "So for example, for an image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 278.99,
          "end": 281.68,
          "en": "it by default renders the image element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 281.68,
          "end": 285.34000000000003,
          "en": "and we can target an image property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 285.34000000000003,
          "end": 289.21,
          "en": "in our renderers object if we wanna override it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 289.21,
          "end": 292.23,
          "en": "So renderers are, let's say customRenderers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 293.7,
          "end": 295.27,
          "en": "is an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 295.27,
          "end": 297.33,
          "en": "That's what we should pass to renderers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 297.33,
          "end": 300.337,
          "en": "if we wanna override some renderers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 300.337,
          "end": 303.65,
          "en": "And in this object we can now target identifiers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 303.65,
          "end": 304.703,
          "en": "like image here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 305.95,
          "end": 306.783,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 306.783,
          "end": 308.6,
          "en": "And set them as a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 308.6,
          "end": 311.33,
          "en": "or to be precise, as a method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 311.33,
          "end": 314.66,
          "en": "And react-markdown will call this method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 314.66,
          "end": 318.49,
          "en": "if it finds a image in the Markdown content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 318.49,
          "end": 321.16,
          "en": "We can do this for other kinds of elements as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 321.16,
          "end": 322.093,
          "en": "as you see here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 323.34,
          "end": 325.31,
          "en": "So here I'm interested in an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 325.31,
          "end": 326.65,
          "en": "If we find an image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 326.65,
          "end": 329.47,
          "en": "then I don't wanna use the default image element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 329.47,
          "end": 332.27,
          "en": "but instead this method will be called.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 332.27,
          "end": 336.29,
          "en": "In this method, we get data about the image which was found",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 336.29,
          "end": 339.92,
          "en": "and here we then should return our own JSX element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 339.92,
          "end": 341.67,
          "en": "So we could return the built-in image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 341.67,
          "end": 345.44,
          "en": "but then we just do what react-markdown does anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 345.44,
          "end": 347.69,
          "en": "And we set the src and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 347.69,
          "end": 349.39,
          "en": "That's not what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 349.39,
          "end": 353.28,
          "en": "Instead, I'll return the Next.js image element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 353.28,
          "end": 355.54,
          "en": "the Next.js image component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 355.54,
          "end": 358.42,
          "en": "which we therefore, of course, also need to import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 358.42,
          "end": 362.033,
          "en": "We import Image from next/image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 363.07,
          "end": 364.71,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 364.71,
          "end": 366.83,
          "en": "So that's what we return here then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 366.83,
          "end": 369.99,
          "en": "and then we set the src to something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 369.99,
          "end": 371.73,
          "en": "the alt text to something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 371.73,
          "end": 375.3,
          "en": "and also width and height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 375.3,
          "end": 376.72,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 376.72,
          "end": 379.17,
          "en": "Now, let's start with alt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 379.17,
          "end": 382.92,
          "en": "The image which we get here is actually an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 382.92,
          "end": 386.72,
          "en": "with the image data react-markdown got",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 386.72,
          "end": 388.49,
          "en": "from the Markdown text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 388.49,
          "end": 390.75,
          "en": "And the alt text, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 390.75,
          "end": 394.573,
          "en": "in Markdown is the text between those square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 396.24,
          "end": 398.6,
          "en": "So that is already made available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 398.6,
          "end": 403.6,
          "en": "by react-markdown and hence, we can set alt to image.alt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 406.05,
          "end": 409.32,
          "en": "The name, the URL of the image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 409.32,
          "end": 412.9,
          "en": "so the thing between the parentheses, this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 412.9,
          "end": 415.82,
          "en": "is also made available by react-markdown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 415.82,
          "end": 417.95,
          "en": "It's also available on this image object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 417.95,
          "end": 419.93,
          "en": "and it's the image.url.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 419.93,
          "end": 422.66,
          "en": "But that's just a file name in our case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 422.66,
          "end": 424.68,
          "en": "We need a full path here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 424.68,
          "end": 427.2,
          "en": "and for that, I'll create a template literal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 427.2,
          "end": 432.2,
          "en": "where I point at images/posts/post.slug,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 432.51,
          "end": 434.47,
          "en": "so the slug for this loaded post,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 434.47,
          "end": 437.183,
          "en": "slash and then this URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 438.06,
          "end": 441.7,
          "en": "this file name which was stored in the Markdown file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 441.7,
          "end": 444.33,
          "en": "So in this case, image.url.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 444.33,
          "end": 445.81,
          "en": "So now that's that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 445.81,
          "end": 447.05,
          "en": "Now, for width and height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 447.05,
          "end": 450.66700000000003,
          "en": "it always comes down to how you present this to your styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 450.66700000000003,
          "end": 451.5,
          "en": "and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 451.5,
          "end": 453.8,
          "en": "Here a width of 600 and a height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 453.8,
          "end": 457.65999999999997,
          "en": "of 300 pixels should work quite well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 457.65999999999997,
          "end": 461.34000000000003,
          "en": "Now with that, since we pass customRenderers to renderers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 461.34000000000003,
          "end": 465.683,
          "en": "this next image will be rendered instead of a default image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 467.01,
          "end": 468.83,
          "en": "If we save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 468.83,
          "end": 471.483,
          "en": "and reload, that fails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 472.5,
          "end": 477.47,
          "en": "Actually because it's not image.url but image.src here, src.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 477.47,
          "end": 478.303,
          "en": "My bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 478.303,
          "end": 482.32,
          "en": "So image.src is the property on this image object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 482.32,
          "end": 485.52,
          "en": "which holds a pointer at the image we're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 485.52,
          "end": 487.61,
          "en": "and if we change this to image.src,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 487.61,
          "end": 489.91,
          "en": "we now see our image rendered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 489.91,
          "end": 491.853,
          "en": "with the dimensions we gave it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 492.9,
          "end": 494.728,
          "en": "But if we open the dev tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 494.728,
          "end": 497.87,
          "en": "we'll be greeted with a lot of warnings here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 497.87,
          "end": 499.3,
          "en": "The warning in the end tells us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 499.3,
          "end": 502.11,
          "en": "that we're rendering a div inside of a paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 502.11,
          "end": 503.7,
          "en": "because the next/image element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 503.7,
          "end": 505.88,
          "en": "is actually not just an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 505.88,
          "end": 508.01,
          "en": "Instead, it is wrapped in a couple of divs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 508.01,
          "end": 511.48,
          "en": "which control its positioning and styling and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 511.48,
          "end": 515.9,
          "en": "And that's all rendered automatically by Next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 515.9,
          "end": 518.67,
          "en": "And that's then nested inside of a paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 518.67,
          "end": 521.76,
          "en": "Because Markdown is translated to HTML",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 521.76,
          "end": 524.52,
          "en": "such that all content which is not a title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 524.52,
          "end": 526.4,
          "en": "or a list or something like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 526.4,
          "end": 530.28,
          "en": "is treated as a paragraph, including images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 530.28,
          "end": 532.49,
          "en": "We can ignore this, it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 532.49,
          "end": 534.65,
          "en": "But if we wanna get rid of that error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 534.65,
          "end": 536.13,
          "en": "of that warning, which it is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 536.13,
          "end": 540.4,
          "en": "we can also do that by not overriding the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 540.4,
          "end": 543.21,
          "en": "but by instead getting a bit more tricky.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 543.21,
          "end": 545.81,
          "en": "Instead of only overriding images here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 545.81,
          "end": 546.91,
          "en": "in our customRenderer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 547.96,
          "end": 551.72,
          "en": "we can actually have a look at all paragraphs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 551.72,
          "end": 553.72,
          "en": "which are being rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 553.72,
          "end": 555.13,
          "en": "So this now includes everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 555.13,
          "end": 557.22,
          "en": "which would be rendered as a paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 557.22,
          "end": 561.14,
          "en": "including plain text, like this one or this one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 561.14,
          "end": 563.85,
          "en": "but also images, which as we just saw,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 563.85,
          "end": 566.433,
          "en": "are also rendered as paragraphs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 567.77,
          "end": 569.56,
          "en": "Then here we still get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 569.56,
          "end": 572.88,
          "en": "that paragraph identified by react-markdown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 572.88,
          "end": 576.27,
          "en": "and we can return our own JSX element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 576.27,
          "end": 581.05,
          "en": "And here the trick is that I only wanna override the default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 581.05,
          "end": 583.82,
          "en": "if we actually find that a image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 583.82,
          "end": 586.36,
          "en": "would be rendered inside of the paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 586.36,
          "end": 589.773,
          "en": "and I will leave all other kinds of paragraphs alone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 590.72,
          "end": 593.97,
          "en": "For this, we can extract the actual node",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 593.97,
          "end": 596.47,
          "en": "which would be rendered by react-markdown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 596.47,
          "end": 601.4,
          "en": "from paragraph and then check if the node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 601.4,
          "end": 603.993,
          "en": "if the first child of that node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 604.91,
          "end": 607.05,
          "en": "if the type of that is image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 607.05,
          "end": 610.17,
          "en": "So if we are trying to render a image element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 224,
          "start": 610.17,
          "end": 613.52,
          "en": "as a direct child of that paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 225,
          "start": 613.52,
          "end": 616.45,
          "en": "If we do render an image inside of the paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 226,
          "start": 616.45,
          "end": 620.36,
          "en": "I will override what react-markdown wants to render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 227,
          "start": 620.36,
          "end": 623.24,
          "en": "and instead of rendering a paragraph with the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 228,
          "start": 623.24,
          "end": 627.27,
          "en": "inside of it, I then instead want to render just an image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 229,
          "start": 627.27,
          "end": 629.72,
          "en": "just my next image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 230,
          "start": 629.72,
          "end": 631.47,
          "en": "So for this, I'll then get my image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 231,
          "start": 631.47,
          "end": 635.66,
          "en": "by accessing node.children and then the first child",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 232,
          "start": 635.66,
          "end": 638.42,
          "en": "and then I'll return a div actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 233,
          "start": 638.42,
          "end": 643.17,
          "en": "with some extra styling where I add a class of image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 234,
          "start": 643.17,
          "end": 647.333,
          "en": "That's simply a class I defined here in the CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 235,
          "start": 648.55,
          "end": 651.59,
          "en": "And in there, I'll then render this next image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 236,
          "start": 651.59,
          "end": 654.72,
          "en": "So here I'll just repeat the code from up there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 237,
          "start": 654.72,
          "end": 659.693,
          "en": "grab that code, add it here like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 238,
          "start": 660.79,
          "end": 661.873,
          "en": "And we're good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 239,
          "start": 662.83,
          "end": 665.44,
          "en": "Now we can get rid of this customRenderer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 240,
          "start": 665.44,
          "end": 668.08,
          "en": "and I'll comment it out so that we still see it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 241,
          "start": 668.08,
          "end": 669.56,
          "en": "but will not use it anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 242,
          "start": 669.56,
          "end": 671.82,
          "en": "because we will now change image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 243,
          "start": 671.82,
          "end": 673.3,
          "en": "by looking into paragraphs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 244,
          "start": 673.3,
          "end": 674.97,
          "en": "and looking for images there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 245,
          "start": 674.97,
          "end": 677.18,
          "en": "and then replacing the entire paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 246,
          "start": 677.18,
          "end": 678.833,
          "en": "with a div with the image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 247,
          "start": 679.89,
          "end": 683.16,
          "en": "Now, otherwise, if we don't make it into this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 248,
          "start": 683.16,
          "end": 688.16,
          "en": "I will return a regular paragraph with paragraph.children",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 249,
          "start": 689.66,
          "end": 690.98,
          "en": "inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 250,
          "start": 690.98,
          "end": 694.51,
          "en": "So I'll basically render what react-markdown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 251,
          "start": 694.51,
          "end": 696.12,
          "en": "would have rendered otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 252,
          "start": 696.12,
          "end": 697.36,
          "en": "So I'll just use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 253,
          "start": 697.36,
          "end": 700.77,
          "en": "that unchanged content it identified wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 254,
          "start": 700.77,
          "end": 702.223,
          "en": "in a regular paragraph.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 255,
          "start": 703.21,
          "end": 706.7,
          "en": "If we do this and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 256,
          "start": 706.7,
          "end": 708.7,
          "en": "the image is broken simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 257,
          "start": 708.7,
          "end": 712.163,
          "en": "because here it's now actually not image.src but image.url.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 258,
          "start": 713.76,
          "end": 716.36,
          "en": "That can be confusing but it is different here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 259,
          "start": 716.36,
          "end": 718.81,
          "en": "when we're not handing just a image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 260,
          "start": 718.81,
          "end": 721.69,
          "en": "but a paragraph that may contain an image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 261,
          "start": 721.69,
          "end": 724.76,
          "en": "Then the image, which we get from inside the paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 262,
          "start": 724.76,
          "end": 728.24,
          "en": "has the file name stored in a URL property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 263,
          "start": 728.24,
          "end": 731.71,
          "en": "instead of src but with that it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 264,
          "start": 731.71,
          "end": 735.25,
          "en": "And that's now the image presented on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 265,
          "start": 735.25,
          "end": 739.01,
          "en": "Now rendered again with Next.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 266,
          "start": 739.01,
          "end": 741.63,
          "en": "as we can tell by the complex structure here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 267,
          "start": 741.63,
          "end": 744.1,
          "en": "and the fact that different images are fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 268,
          "start": 744.1,
          "end": 746.44,
          "en": "for different screen resolutions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 269,
          "start": 746.44,
          "end": 748.53,
          "en": "and in the console if we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 270,
          "start": 748.53,
          "end": 750.81,
          "en": "we have no warnings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 271,
          "start": 750.81,
          "end": 752.54,
          "en": "And that's how we can override",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 272,
          "start": 752.54,
          "end": 755.03,
          "en": "how certain elements are rendered.",
